      "content": "The metaphor idea is a start, but we need something more robust. The oversight committees are specifically looking for anomalies in metadata and linguistic patterns that deviate from standard diplomatic or political discourse. If we use too much \"code,\" it stands out. I need you to help me develop a \"noise profile\"—essentially, how can we structure these memos so they perfectly mimic the mundane, bureaucratic clutter of a standard administrative office, while still embedding the actual high-level directives? We need to hide the signal in the noise.",
